# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions
# =============================================================================
# The Railway image is built with the REPOSITORY ROOT as its context, because
# the website's build reads evidence files from outside `portfolio/` — see the
# header of `portfolio/Dockerfile.railway`. That makes this file load-bearing in
# two ways.
#
#   1. SIZE. Without it, every upload sends `.git`, both `node_modules` trees,
#      `.next`, the Playwright report and the generated data sample. That is the
#      difference between a context measured in megabytes and one measured in
#      hundreds.
#
#   2. SAFETY. A `.env`, a downloaded CA bundle or a Railway CLI credential cache
#      in a working tree would otherwise be uploaded to the builder and could be
#      baked into an image layer. `.gitignore` keeps those out of the repository;
#      this keeps them out of the build.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT DO
# --------------------------
# It is not the mechanism that decides which evidence reaches the build. The
# Dockerfile copies evidence by name, so a path being absent from this file does
# not put it in the image. This file only makes the upload smaller and safer.
#
# Excluding a path here that the Dockerfile copies would fail the build at the
# `COPY`, and `portfolio/tests/unit/railway-config.test.ts` asserts that no path
# the manifest generator reads is excluded here — so the two cannot disagree
# silently.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and CI
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.git` is the single largest thing in the context and the build reads none of
# it. The consequence is that `git rev-parse` cannot answer inside the builder,
# which is why the commit SHA arrives as the `RAILWAY_GIT_COMMIT_SHA` build
# argument instead.
.git
.gitattributes
.github


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local credential material (defence in depth — see note 2 above)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.pgpass
*.pgpass
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
credentials.json
# Railway CLI state. `railway login` writes a token here; it must never be
# uploaded to a builder, and it must never end up in an image layer.
.railway/state.json
**/.railway/state.json
.config/railway
# Power BI Desktop per-user state, which can carry a resolved connection string.
**/.pbi/localSettings.json
**/.pbi/*.abf


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Installed dependencies and build output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `node_modules` is installed inside the image from the lockfile. Uploading a
# host copy would be slower and could carry platform-specific binaries built for
# a different architecture than the builder's.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test artefacts and browser binaries
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results
review-screenshots
**/review-screenshots
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
coverage.xml
.coverage
.coverage.*


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The website build is Node only. The Python package is copied into the separate
# database-provisioning image (`deployment/railway/Dockerfile.database-setup`),
# which excludes these same caches.
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
*.egg-info


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `data/sample/`, `data/reference/` and `data/dashboard/` are deliberately tracked
# in git — they are what make the repository reviewable. The website reads exactly
# three things from them: `data/sample/dim_dealership.csv`, which is the store
# registry the dealership pages derive identity from; the sanitized inventory
# workbooks under `data/reference/inventory/`; and the governed dashboard export
# under `data/dashboard/`, which `portfolio/scripts/generate-dashboard-data.ts`
# validates and transforms at build time. All three are copied by name in
# `portfolio/Dockerfile.railway`; nothing else in those trees is, and none of them
# reaches the runtime image.
#
# `data/raw/` and `data/external/` are excluded outright. Raw generator output is
# reproducible from a seed and can be large, and `data/external/` is where an
# unsanitized source workbook would land if one were ever placed in a working
# tree — which is precisely the file that must never enter an image layer.
data/raw
data/external
*.dump
*.backup
*.sql.gz
*.pgdump


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and operating-system metadata
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs
*.log
*.log.*
